@startuml
title AISafe - Create Scheduled Flight (US212)\nCross-service coordination over HTTPS/REST

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "ATCC" as Client
participant "route-1\n:8071" as Route
database "H2\nroute1" as RouteDB
participant "route-2\n:8072" as Peer
participant "aircraft-service\n(8081 / 8082)" as Aircraft
participant "airport-service\n(8091 / 8092)" as Airport
participant "maintenance-service\n(8061 / 8062)" as Maintenance

Client -> Route : POST /api/flights/scheduled\nJWT (role ATCC)\n{routeId, aircraftRegistrationNumber,\n scheduledDeparture, scheduledArrival}
activate Route
Route -> Route : validate JWT, role and input\n(arrival after departure)
Route -> RouteDB : find Route by routeId
note right of Route : if the route is not stored locally,\nit is fetched from route-2 (forwarding rule)
Route -> Route : route must be ACTIVE;\nread requiredRange, requiredCapacity,\norigin and destination IATA codes

Route -> Aircraft : GET /api/hangar/aircraft/{registrationNumber}\nJWT + X-Service-Key
Aircraft --> Route : 200 {status, modelName,\nmaximumRangeKm, seatingCapacity}

Route -> Airport : GET /api/airports/{originIata}
Airport --> Route : 200 {status, certifications}
Route -> Airport : GET /api/airports/{destinationIata}
Airport --> Route : 200 {status, certifications}

Route -> Maintenance : GET /api/maintenance/aircraft/{registrationNumber}/ongoing
Maintenance --> Route : 200 {underMaintenance: false}

group Overlap check across replicas (aggregation)
  Route -> RouteDB : flights of aircraft in [departure, arrival]
  Route -> Peer : GET /api/flights/aircraft/{registrationNumber}\nX-Forwarded-By: route-1 + X-Service-Key
  Peer --> Route : 200 flights stored on route-2
end

alt All checks pass
  Route -> RouteDB : save Flight (UUID, status SCHEDULED)\n+ increment RouteHistory (same local transaction)
  Route -> Route : audit log: user, action, flightId, instance
  Route --> Client : 201 Created + Location /api/flights/{id}
else Business rule violated
  note over Route
    aircraft not AVAILABLE, under maintenance,
    range < requiredRange, capacity < requiredCapacity,
    airport not OPERATIONAL or overlapping flight
  end note
  Route --> Client : 409 Conflict + reason
else Aircraft, airport or route not found
  Route --> Client : 404 Not Found + which resource
else Provider service or route peer unreachable (both replicas, after retries)
  Route --> Client : 503 Service Unavailable\n(flight NOT created)
end
deactivate Route

legend bottom left
  The provider replica that receives each call may itself forward it to its peer
  (aircraft, airport and maintenance data are partitioned between replicas).
  Calls to another service try replica 1 first and fail over to replica 2 (connect 1 s, read 2 s).
  Reads favour availability, but creating a flight requires complete answers: if a check
  cannot be completed the write is refused (503) instead of risking an unsafe assignment.
  Contracts added for SIDIS: AircraftResponse gains maximumRangeKm and seatingCapacity;
  maintenance-service exposes GET /api/maintenance/aircraft/{registrationNumber}/ongoing.
  Known limitation: airport Certification does not reference an aircraft model (PSOFT US106a),
  so model-to-airport eligibility is not validated; only airport status is checked.
endlegend
@enduml
